    "FT.": "Redis 8 absorbed RediSearch. kevy has its own index/query surface (INDEX, VIEW, TABLE) designed for this engine rather than a reimplementation of FT.*; parity here is a product decision, not a gap to close by default.",
    "JSON.": "same shape as FT.* — a module Redis absorbed, not core key-space semantics.",
    "TS.": "same shape as FT.* — TimeSeries module.",
    "BF.|CF.|CMS.|TOPK.|TDIGEST.": "probabilistic module family absorbed into Redis 8.",
    "SUBSCRIBE SHARD|SSUBSCRIBE|SUNSUBSCRIBE|SPUBLISH": "shard pub/sub is a cluster feature.",
    "FAILOVER|REPLICAOF|SLAVEOF|PSYNC|SYNC": "kevy has its own replication verbs; the Redis wire-level replication handshake is not a compatibility target.",
